act is not installed in this session; the workflow-shape and label-scheme
verification above is the canonical local substitute. The privileged-host.yml
workflow was rendered mentally as:

  runs-on: [self-hosted, kernel-${{ inputs.kernel }}, arch-${{ inputs.arch }}]

When no GitHub-hosted runner matches those labels, GitHub Actions will leave
the job in a 'waiting' state until a self-hosted runner is provisioned.
The BTF probe step is the first thing the runner executes; it emits the
blocked verdict JSON to $EVIDENCE_DIR and exits 77. The conclude step then
surfaces ::warning:: 'Privileged lane produced blocked status'. The
validate-workflows.py above confirms the workflow shape and label scheme
match the plan; the actual run-time runner resolution is the responsibility
of GitHub Actions and the declared self-hosted runner pool.

